Compute observed Pearson correlations, estimate a permutation null, and select an empirical FDR threshold
for features to be considered statistically correlated wiht dilution factors.

options:
  -h, --help            
  show this help message and exit

  -i, --input INPUT     
  Path to the tab-delimited intensity matrix input file.

  -o, --output OUTPUT   
  Path to save the intensity table with observed Pearson r and p values.

  -p, --plot PLOT       
  Path to save the diagnostic plot.

  -c, --correlation_type 
    Choose type of the correlation coefficient. Options: 
        - Pearson correlation (pearson), default
        - Spearman correlation (spearman)

  -n, --n-permutations N_PERMUTATIONS
  Number of random permutations to generate the null distribution.

  -f, --target-fdr TARGET_FDR
  Target empirical false discovery rate for threshold selection.

  --seed SEED           
  Random seed for permutation sampling.

  --id-col ID_COL       
  Name of the feature identifier column in the input table.

  --results-dir RESULTS_DIR
  Directory where output files will be saved. Defaults to a subfolder next to the input file.